Generate one unrestricted TLS credential for each notification service
test and reuse it across connections and server restarts. tls 2.4
rejects the server-only fixture for client authentication, while
generating a new credential for every connection changes the SMP service
identity.

Read service-subscription metrics strictly. The lazy reader leaves the
handle locked while the periodic writer reopens it; its resource-busy
exception terminates the server and makes the client fail with TLS EOF.

Index: tests/ServerTests.hs
